From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:30:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: sync the AVD driver with aurora
 integration/aurora

Bring drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/ and the apple,avd binding to
aurora-silicon/linux integration/aurora at
commit 9c607045fa7c ("Merge pull request #1244 from aurora-silicon/tb3/xdomain-no-rebond")
(2026-11-08). The tree carried the AVD of the omacom pin, which matches
integration/aurora of 2026-10-23 at
commit 4e5eea54ce7e ("Merge pull request #368 from jgoyvaerts/m4pro/small-fixes")
except for avd-drv.c. The 85 integration commits since then are listed
below. They include the v5 HEVC header split, the legacy-transport
hardening (no empty mailbox pops, an error storm rests the decoder instead
of resetting it in a loop, DMA stays blocked after retirement), the queued
transport for the open firmware (the legacy transport stays for firmware
without the queued ABI, such as avd-fw 0.1), FFmpeg's HEVC slice layout,
B-only temporal-direct and mvd_l1_zero bits, flat H.264 scaling lists, AV1
reference and tile bounds, and the PMC performance floor this tree already
carried.

Every file under drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/ and apple,avd.yaml is
byte-identical to that integration commit. The v4l2-mem2mem part of
commit 6e3a36cd298e ("media: v4l2-mem2mem: support detached buffers for pipelined dispatch")
is the previous commit.

This is a file-level sync because the integration history between the two
states runs through parallel branches with duplicate and reverted commits
(the same mailbox fix landed twice, and one AV1 overlap change was reverted
and reapplied; all are in the list), which do not replay as a linear
series.

